capability map/range-of-keys  the entries whose keys lie between two bounds, found without a walk
  heroes  refused: the language's map finds by hash and keeps insertion order, so it has no index sorted by key to cut; a range is a walk of `sort(keys(m))` with the comparison the key's type has, and a map kept in the order of its keys, Rust's `BTreeMap`, is `containers/ordered`, whose `slots_between` walks a range and `floor_slot` and `ceiling_slot` find the keys around a bound at the cost of the logarithm of the size
  go      -
  rust    BTreeMap::range, BTreeMap::range_mut, BTreeMap::split_off, BTreeMap::lower_bound, BTreeMap::lower_bound_mut, BTreeMap::upper_bound, BTreeMap::upper_bound_mut, btree_map::Cursor, btree_map::CursorMut, btree_map::CursorMutKey
  python  -
  note    -

